1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:32,095
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:39,330
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

3
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:48,923
Kang Pi-o, let's make a promise.

4
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:50,967
After the competition is over,

5
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:53,678
let's hang out and play some more four-hands.

6
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:54,804
Okay.

7
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:11,321
He slipped out in the middle of the event and went into some random practice room,

8
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:13,865
and just stared out of the window from behind the curtains.

9
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:20,246
He seemed really flustered when I walked in.

10
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:21,164
Could it be

11
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:23,458
that he got his memories back?

12
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:37,514
Hey, don't be sore if I beat you, okay? When we play, let's have fun!

13
00:01:37,597 --> 00:01:39,682
Oh, please. I'm the one who's gonna win!

14
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:40,934
So you can't get upset.

15
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:58,118
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

16
00:01:59,619 --> 00:02:00,954
EPISODE 10

17
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:39,284
N N

18
00:02:39,784 --> 00:02:40,869
N

19
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,248
I can come in, right?

20
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:56,342
What are you doing here this late, out of the blue?

21
00:02:58,761 --> 00:02:59,596
What?

22
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:02,640
Do you have any questions about the piece?

23
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:04,309
Mm-hmm.

24
00:03:05,185 --> 00:03:06,019
What is it?

25
00:03:07,353 --> 00:03:09,355
Have you not figured out the tempo yet?

26
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:10,398
You started…

27
00:03:11,691 --> 00:03:13,776
composing the piece five years ago, yeah?

28
00:03:14,777 --> 00:03:16,487
Took me about five years to finish.

29
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:17,530
Mr. Kang…

30
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:19,991
would you premiere this piece?

31
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:23,244
You lost

32
00:03:24,704 --> 00:03:26,956
your memories after the accident, didn't you?

33
00:03:28,124 --> 00:03:28,958
Yes.

34
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:30,627
What's your point?

35
00:03:31,878 --> 00:03:33,296
Is there some sort of issue?

36
00:03:35,131 --> 00:03:37,967
What did you mean when you said I haven't changed a bit?

37
00:03:39,302 --> 00:03:42,597
Mr. Kang Pi-o, how is it that you haven't changed one bit?

38
00:03:43,223 --> 00:03:45,225
What point in time were you referring to?

39
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:46,643
The time in high school?

40
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:48,478
Or the one in Prague?

41
00:03:50,146 --> 00:03:51,522
What are you trying to tell me?

42
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:55,235
How much longer are you going to keep pretending you don't remember?

43
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:58,863
Mr. Kang Pi-o, I'm afraid I don't understand what you mean by that.

44
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:00,365
N

45
00:04:00,865 --> 00:04:02,367
Then what do you make of this?

46
00:04:03,409 --> 00:04:05,328
Back in high school, I happened to see

47
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:07,789
a draft of a piece in your dorm room.

48
00:04:07,872 --> 00:04:08,706
It had exactly

49
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:11,417
the same main theme as "Nemesis."

50
00:04:13,336 --> 00:04:14,212
Really?

51
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:18,174
Wow, I didn't know I could write something like that in high school.

52
00:04:18,841 --> 00:04:19,676
I guess

53
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:23,680
losing your memory doesn't mean you're losing every part of yourself.

54
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:26,266
So,

55
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:30,603
you do remember the practice room where we met?

56
00:04:32,021 --> 00:04:32,855
Or is that

57
00:04:34,023 --> 00:04:35,191
all just a coincidence?

58
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,280
Just stop it,

59
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:42,115
Choi Jeong-yo.

60
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:46,494
You remember everything.

61
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:49,497
N

62
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:52,458
That's right.

63
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:55,795
N

64
00:04:57,588 --> 00:04:58,423
The truth is,

65
00:05:00,758 --> 00:05:02,093
I really wanted to see it.

66
00:05:03,469 --> 00:05:05,388
That practice room where we first met.

67
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,392
That Hungarian Dance we played together.

68
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:11,185
Danse macabre.

69
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,022
Even the noise in the hallway.

70
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:18,818
I have never forgotten any of it.

71
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:21,154
Why'd you do it?

72
00:05:24,073 --> 00:05:26,075
Why the hell lie to me like that Jeong-yo?

73
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:27,201
You know why.

74
00:05:29,245 --> 00:05:31,164
If I had said I remembered everything,

75
00:05:31,956 --> 00:05:34,459
you would've tried to kill me again, wouldn't you?

76
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:38,796
What do you mean?

77
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:41,924
Why would you say I'd try to kill you?

78
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:43,468
Do you think I'm an idiot?

79
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:45,595
I know that you were the one who

80
00:05:45,678 --> 00:05:48,765
had me kidnapped during the competition nine years ago.

81
00:05:49,557 --> 00:05:51,267
Don't pretend like you don't know.

82
00:05:52,643 --> 00:05:55,897
I saw you meeting the man who kidnapped me, with my own two eyes.

83
00:05:57,273 --> 00:05:59,150
At first, I just couldn't believe it.

84
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:05,698
Of all people, you were the one I trusted the most.

85
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:06,616
N

86
00:06:07,116 --> 00:06:09,369
No one with a shred of decency would do this.

87
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:14,582
Kang Pi-o.

88
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:16,084
He put us up to it.

89
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:17,543
But then…

90
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:20,880
one of the bastards who kidnapped me said your name.

91
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:25,093
Is there an international bank close by here?

92
00:06:25,885 --> 00:06:28,096
Huh? You wanna come back?

93
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:34,435
And I also got to see you pay off another one of them.

94
00:06:35,144 --> 00:06:36,854
I even went to see you perform.

95
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:39,399
It was clear… N

96
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:42,610
that you had already completely forgotten about me.

97
00:06:44,779 --> 00:06:47,448
You played the piano as if nothing had ever happened.

98
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:53,079
How was it? All this time?

99
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:57,875
Did you feel like you could breathe after I was gone?

100
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:00,795
How did it feel to stand in the winner's seat?

101
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:02,004
Did it feel good?

102
00:07:12,765 --> 00:07:13,808
N

103
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:16,436
Why did you do that to me?

104
00:07:18,729 --> 00:07:20,189
No!

105
00:07:21,023 --> 00:07:22,191
I'd rather kill myself.

106
00:07:23,025 --> 00:07:25,862
Then let this ever see the light of day. So…

107
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:27,864
you gonna let me commit suicide?

108
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:43,504
I'm sorry.

109
00:07:46,757 --> 00:07:47,592
You're right.

110
00:07:49,802 --> 00:07:50,636
I did it.

111
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:59,729
After I hurt my finger after the final round, I couldn't think straight.

112
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:03,024
I poured everything I had into that competition,

113
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:06,027
and I was afraid I wouldn't place first because of you.

114
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:07,445
And for what I did to you,

115
00:08:08,821 --> 00:08:10,490
I'll turn myself in immediately.

116
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:13,367
I'll take responsibility…

117
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:15,328
for all of it.

118
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:16,996
You will?

119
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:20,875
So after ruining my life… you

120
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:23,961
think that rotting in jail will be enough?

121
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:25,421
N

122
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:29,759
Do you really think I came back after all this just to let you off the hook?

123
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:30,968
Hey.

124
00:08:33,179 --> 00:08:34,889
If punishment is to be dealt out,

125
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:37,600
It will definitely come from me.

126
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:40,478
Then will that be the end of it?

127
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:41,979
No.

128
00:08:43,564 --> 00:08:45,650
I don't plan on letting it end like that.

129
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:52,114
The moment you take the easy way out, your crimes will be exposed to the world,

130
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:55,868
and your accomplice of a mother won't be able to get away with it either.

131
00:08:58,371 --> 00:09:01,165
Just wait. I'm gonna make your life hell.

132
00:09:03,834 --> 00:09:06,921
Whatever you're thinking, it's gonna be much worse than that.

133
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:19,475
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE TRADITIONAL MARKET

134
00:09:29,902 --> 00:09:32,405
Hello, how are you, sir? Um,

135
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:34,073
-may I ask you a quick question? -Sure.

136
00:09:34,156 --> 00:09:34,991
Do you…

137
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:37,493
happen to know who this is?

138
00:09:38,077 --> 00:09:40,288
He's Conductor Choi Jeong-yo. Didn't he grow up here?

139
00:09:40,371 --> 00:09:42,832
Oh, I think I do remember him. Yeah.

140
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:43,874
Then

141
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:45,376
would you happen to know

142
00:09:45,459 --> 00:09:46,961
where his father is?

143
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:48,838
I don't know.

144
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:51,799
Thanks for your time.

145
00:10:02,727 --> 00:10:03,853
See, it's right there.

146
00:10:08,232 --> 00:10:09,358
Oh, that looks so fresh today!

147
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:10,484
Yeah, we just brought it in.

148
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:11,402
Excuse me.

149
00:10:11,485 --> 00:10:14,113
Do you happen to know Conductor Choi Jeong-yo?

150
00:10:14,905 --> 00:10:18,242
I heard that Jeong-yo's father used to work around here somewhere.

151
00:10:19,827 --> 00:10:20,745
Wait, who is that?

152
00:10:21,954 --> 00:10:24,206
He does look a bit familiar to me…

153
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,124
Oh…

154
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:28,252
Then again, maybe not. I'll be honest, I'm not sure.

155
00:10:29,545 --> 00:10:30,379
I have no idea.

156
00:10:38,387 --> 00:10:39,221
Excuse me.

157
00:10:42,391 --> 00:10:43,559
You know Choi Jeong-yo?

158
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:53,944
So…

159
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:57,156
-What was your name? -General Manager Kim.

160
00:10:58,574 --> 00:11:00,159
-Who are you? -Oh,

161
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:01,661
I'm…

162
00:11:02,578 --> 00:11:04,121
Jeong-yo's friend's mother.

163
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:05,539
I don't

164
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:09,168
know if you saw it on the news, but poor Jeong-yo has lost his memories.

165
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:12,296
So I'm trying to find someone from his family to help.

166
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:13,839
Oh.

167
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:16,008
So you're trying to help?

168
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:19,178
How is it that…

169
00:11:21,138 --> 00:11:22,723
the two of you know each other?

170
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:24,475
We were close friends.

171
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:26,769
Ah.

172
00:11:27,645 --> 00:11:29,480
That's great. So…

173
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:31,107
do you happen to know

174
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,567
where his father might be now?

175
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,153
That bastard owes me money.

176
00:11:36,696 --> 00:11:38,322
I could probably track him down.

177
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:41,283
He's probably out, getting drunk somewhere.

178
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:45,246
N

179
00:11:48,999 --> 00:11:52,002
ALCOHOL ADDICTION TREATMENT CENTER

180
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:56,549
Oh, um…

181
00:11:58,050 --> 00:12:01,846
So you're telling me you also don't know where his father might be, right?

182
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:04,098
Thank you for your time today.

183
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:05,599
I should get going.

184
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:21,157
You're Pianist Kang Pi-o's mother, aren't you?

185
00:12:21,907 --> 00:12:23,033
I saw you on the news.

186
00:12:24,368 --> 00:12:25,703
When Jeong-yo was kidnapped,

187
00:12:25,786 --> 00:12:27,329
and Pianist Kang Pi-o won.

188
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:29,165
You know…

189
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:32,084
if you poke around, people will know.

190
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:39,717
If you ever need any help, call me.

191
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:54,231
Just pick up the phone!

192
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:58,360
-Pi-o. -Yes?

193
00:12:58,861 --> 00:12:59,945
I'm scared.

194
00:13:01,864 --> 00:13:02,698
Choi Jeong-yo…

195
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:05,493
has never had amnesia.

196
00:13:06,994 --> 00:13:08,621
His father is an alcoholic.

197
00:13:08,704 --> 00:13:10,664
He went to see him at that hospital.

198
00:13:13,793 --> 00:13:16,629
I know he's doing this to get back at us. What do we do?

199
00:13:17,463 --> 00:13:19,548
He'll expose us, if we don't do anything.

200
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:22,134
We have to stop him at all costs.

201
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:25,054
No matter what it takes, do you understand?

202
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:26,305
Why should we stop him?

203
00:13:26,806 --> 00:13:28,015
We're the ones at fault.

204
00:13:28,849 --> 00:13:31,018
All he'd be doing is telling the truth.

205
00:13:31,101 --> 00:13:33,646
We have to get rid of him so that he can't run his mouth.

206
00:13:33,729 --> 00:13:34,980
What are you saying?

207
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:37,233
We have no other choice if we want to stay alive!

208
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:38,901
Please, just stop it!

209
00:13:40,152 --> 00:13:42,071
If you ever lay a finger on him again,

210
00:13:43,864 --> 00:13:47,409
-I swear, I won't just sit back and watch. -Are you out of your mind?

211
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:49,286
Did you not hear what I told you?

212
00:13:49,829 --> 00:13:52,748
He came back just to get revenge on us, do you hear me?

213
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:54,708
Then I will be the one to bear it.

214
00:13:56,043 --> 00:13:58,295
-It's what I need to do. -Pi-o!

215
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:05,261
I feel

216
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:08,264
that this contract is heavily stacked against the soloist.

217
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:09,890
If we accept this clause,

218
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:13,936
the risk for the soloist would be way too much if the project falls through.

219
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:17,356
We're assuming a lot of risk here by signing this contract as well.

220
00:14:17,439 --> 00:14:18,983
A world-premiere recording

221
00:14:19,066 --> 00:14:21,569
is different from recording standard repertoire.

222
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:22,528
I do think,

223
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:24,905
this is a bit excessive, don't you?

224
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:27,616
The Soloist Replacement clause…

225
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:32,329
Well, as you know, that's just a safeguard for a worst-case scenario.

226
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:35,541
If the recording is delayed because of the artist,

227
00:14:35,624 --> 00:14:38,502
it disrupts the entire schedule, including the concert hall rental,

228
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,212
the orchestra, and the engineering crew.

229
00:14:40,296 --> 00:14:43,007
We're just trying to minimize our losses. To be frank…

230
00:14:43,883 --> 00:14:47,219
it's mostly just a formality, but for legal reasons and our protection,

231
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:49,555
we have to add this clause to every contract.

232
00:14:51,515 --> 00:14:53,726
Yes, I absolutely understand what you're saying.

233
00:14:53,809 --> 00:14:56,562
We will discuss it internally and then get back to you.

234
00:15:11,452 --> 00:15:12,661
Why did you do that for?

235
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:15,998
We we're gonna make them remove the one-sided clauses.

236
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:17,333
Why sign in such a hurry?

237
00:15:18,417 --> 00:15:19,251
It's fine.

238
00:15:19,793 --> 00:15:20,920
I gotta do a good job.

239
00:15:21,962 --> 00:15:22,880
There's no time.

240
00:15:25,382 --> 00:15:26,842
When the schedule's finalized,

241
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:30,054
I'll put together a list of tonmeisters and send it your way.

242
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:33,223
We will try to get Dominic, because he's the best in the business.

243
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:35,476
Since we don't know what his schedule's like,

244
00:15:35,559 --> 00:15:37,269
I'll have a list ready for you

245
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:38,854
of other potential candidates.

246
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,606
Thanks for doing that.

247
00:15:41,815 --> 00:15:42,650
Gosh,

248
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:45,527
now that we've signed the contract, I'm getting nervous.

249
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:48,405
On that note, we should increase your practice time.

250
00:15:49,239 --> 00:15:51,533
I know the orchestra is in pretty good shape,

251
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:54,536
but the solo's still feeling quite shaky.

252
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:58,165
What do you think? N

253
00:15:58,707 --> 00:15:59,875
Can you make the time?

254
00:16:00,834 --> 00:16:01,669
Of course.

255
00:16:02,586 --> 00:16:04,964
Hey, since we still have a few things iron out,

256
00:16:05,631 --> 00:16:08,133
don't bring your accompanist. Come by yourself.

257
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:11,136
Can I count on you?

258
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:28,821
What…

259
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:31,407
is gonna happen to us?

260
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:37,329
Should we just sit around and wait for our lives to be over?

261
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:39,248
I will figure something out.

262
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:42,793
You don't need to worry.

263
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:06,025
Come in.

264
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:26,670
Wait.

265
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:29,965
At this tempo.

266
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:32,009
Why do it so fast?

267
00:17:32,968 --> 00:17:34,470
I think what's important for the opening

268
00:17:34,553 --> 00:17:36,972
of this piece is to evoke an emotional resonance.

269
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:39,183
I don't think it's about the tempo at all.

270
00:17:40,392 --> 00:17:42,644
Do you think I even care about your opinion?

271
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:43,645
N

272
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:47,524
I already have a very clear vision in my head of the sound and tempo I want,

273
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:49,985
and you clearly don't have enough power to do it.

274
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,070
I want this piece

275
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:54,281
to erupt with explosive, concentrated power,

276
00:17:55,365 --> 00:17:57,534
not collapse into something weak and limp.

277
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,036
Understood?

278
00:18:51,588 --> 00:18:52,422
Again.

279
00:18:53,507 --> 00:18:54,675
Cadenza, at this tempo.

280
00:18:55,717 --> 00:18:57,386
What are you trying to do here?

281
00:18:58,303 --> 00:18:59,138
What?

282
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:01,974
You're trying to ruin my fingers so I can't play?

283
00:19:02,057 --> 00:19:03,767
Is this the revenge you warned me would come?

284
00:19:03,851 --> 00:19:05,811
You really don't get it at all, do you?

285
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:11,900
You know, I think you've got something seriously wrong here.

286
00:19:14,194 --> 00:19:16,363
I didn't entrust you with my precious piece so you

287
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:18,365
could pull some cheap stunt like that.

288
00:19:23,912 --> 00:19:26,373
I had the barrel of a gun aimed right at my head.

289
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:34,089
The car was driving deep into the forest.

290
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:36,800
It was obvious what those bastards were going to do.

291
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:39,887
They were going to drag me off somewhere remote and kill me, leaving no trace.

292
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:41,305
Shut up and just drive!

293
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:44,308
-Before you end up killing us all! -Do what you gotta do.

294
00:19:44,391 --> 00:19:46,268
Just don't get blood all over my car.

295
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:47,978
But then,

296
00:19:48,061 --> 00:19:52,149
a small window of opportunity opened up when they started fighting each other.

297
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:56,028
That was my chance, so I fought for my life and somehow managed to escape.

298
00:19:58,197 --> 00:19:59,031
"Am I safe now?"

299
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:00,782
"Am I free?"

300
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:03,035
For a moment, I thought I was.

301
00:20:03,535 --> 00:20:04,536
And then…

302
00:20:06,121 --> 00:20:09,416
I heard the sound of a bullet tearing through my right shoulder.

303
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:17,758
And that trauma…

304
00:20:20,135 --> 00:20:21,970
left me with amnesia for five years.

305
00:20:23,513 --> 00:20:25,015
Until the day I saw you again.

306
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:27,684
That was it.

307
00:20:29,519 --> 00:20:32,231
That hellish moment is what I captured in the cadenza.

308
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:34,483
Do you really think…

309
00:20:35,859 --> 00:20:39,321
that you're communicating that overwhelming fear in your performance?

310
00:20:41,156 --> 00:20:42,407
Don't get things twisted.

311
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:45,661
I'm not doing this out of spite.

312
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:50,624
Making "Nemesis" a masterpiece matters more to me than it ever will to you.

313
00:20:51,124 --> 00:20:51,959
So I'd say,

314
00:20:53,835 --> 00:20:56,004
instead of worrying about your fingers,

315
00:20:58,465 --> 00:21:02,302
why not worry about properly expressing the composer's vision for the piece?

316
00:21:03,595 --> 00:21:07,224
You really expect me to forgive you when you perform my piece like that?

317
00:21:28,954 --> 00:21:30,789
Four and five have to be stronger.

318
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:33,500
With more clarity, again!

319
00:22:52,537 --> 00:22:54,831
I have to… I have to… find a way.

320
00:23:20,399 --> 00:23:22,150
You still didn't convince me today.

321
00:23:22,776 --> 00:23:25,737
I still don't hear the murderous intent behind the cadenza.

322
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:27,447
PAIN MEDICATION

323
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:53,807
What is the concert hall schedule looking like, Ms. Yoon?

324
00:23:54,641 --> 00:23:55,517
Well, I've checked…

325
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:58,145
our concert hall is fully booked. I barely managed

326
00:23:58,228 --> 00:23:59,479
to free up one day.

327
00:23:59,563 --> 00:24:00,981
Oh… Do you think

328
00:24:01,064 --> 00:24:02,065
that'll be enough?

329
00:24:02,149 --> 00:24:04,443
Uhm… isn't the schedule too tight?

330
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:06,695
Jeong-yo is putting both Pi-o and the orchestra

331
00:24:06,778 --> 00:24:08,947
through some really grueling rehearsals right now.

332
00:24:09,030 --> 00:24:11,199
I think it will be doable in one day.

333
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:13,452
Even on the day, they can record them separately,

334
00:24:13,535 --> 00:24:14,786
so I think we'll be fine.

335
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:17,372
-Wait… how? -Mm?

336
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:19,708
Why do it like that? Uh… now?

337
00:24:20,208 --> 00:24:21,334
Who knows?

338
00:24:22,502 --> 00:24:25,130
Jeong-yo, says it's too early to put them together.

339
00:24:25,213 --> 00:24:26,923
He's using that approach for now.

340
00:24:27,799 --> 00:24:28,675
As the composer,

341
00:24:28,758 --> 00:24:30,177
I'm sure he has his reasons.

342
00:24:33,388 --> 00:24:34,222
Why is it

343
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:37,517
that your playing's gotten dull just because your fingers hurt a little?!

344
00:24:42,939 --> 00:24:45,025
Stop whining and stay focused until the end!

345
00:24:45,108 --> 00:24:45,942
N

346
00:24:50,113 --> 00:24:51,823
N What's going on, Choi Jeong-yo?

347
00:24:52,949 --> 00:24:55,785
He's a professional. Why are you talking to him like this?

348
00:24:55,869 --> 00:24:56,703
Hong Jae-in.

349
00:24:57,996 --> 00:25:00,248
-Why are you barging in like this? -And that tempo?

350
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:02,375
Why are you making him play so fast?

351
00:25:02,459 --> 00:25:05,045
You know it could hurt him to keep playing like that!

352
00:25:05,128 --> 00:25:06,922
What are you doing? Come.

353
00:25:07,005 --> 00:25:07,964
Let's talk outside.

354
00:25:11,092 --> 00:25:13,386
What happened to you?

355
00:25:20,185 --> 00:25:21,144
Hey, Choi Jeong-yo.

356
00:25:22,187 --> 00:25:24,606
-Why are you doing this? -N

357
00:25:24,689 --> 00:25:28,485
With hands in that state, you should've told him to stop practicing and rest!

358
00:25:28,568 --> 00:25:32,155
What if he can't play the piano anymore? You'd be responsible for that.

359
00:25:32,239 --> 00:25:33,114
Step outside.

360
00:25:33,615 --> 00:25:34,533
I said step outside.

361
00:25:34,616 --> 00:25:35,534
Let go of me.

362
00:25:35,617 --> 00:25:36,868
I said let me go!

363
00:25:44,751 --> 00:25:45,669
Explain it to me.

364
00:25:47,003 --> 00:25:47,837
Tell me…

365
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:50,131
why's he treating you like that?

366
00:25:50,215 --> 00:25:52,259
And why are you letting him do that?

367
00:25:52,342 --> 00:25:53,718
Do you owe him something?

368
00:25:54,219 --> 00:25:56,555
Whether I ruin my fingers or the performance,

369
00:25:57,472 --> 00:25:58,306
that's my issue.

370
00:25:58,848 --> 00:26:00,600
So could you please stay out of it.

371
00:26:01,226 --> 00:26:02,060
Hey, Kang Pi-o.

372
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:05,480
I know I'm your girlfriend, but I'm…

373
00:26:05,564 --> 00:26:06,731
your manager first.

374
00:26:07,899 --> 00:26:09,234
Look at the state you're in.

375
00:26:09,317 --> 00:26:13,280
How can you tell me to stay out of it? You should not be performing at all.

376
00:26:13,363 --> 00:26:14,447
This won't work.

377
00:26:15,532 --> 00:26:16,616
We've got to postpone

378
00:26:17,117 --> 00:26:19,327
the recording. Actually, no.

379
00:26:19,953 --> 00:26:21,913
You should pull out of the performance.

380
00:26:22,622 --> 00:26:24,583
The company'll pay the contract penalty,

381
00:26:24,666 --> 00:26:25,709
get out of it.

382
00:26:27,085 --> 00:26:28,336
And the way Choi Jeong-yo

383
00:26:28,962 --> 00:26:32,007
has been pushing you lately isn't normal. His whole approach

384
00:26:32,090 --> 00:26:33,717
is just completely unacceptable.

385
00:26:34,426 --> 00:26:37,262
Maybe I'm not completely on board with his musical vision.

386
00:26:37,345 --> 00:26:39,681
But you're actually playing really well.

387
00:26:39,764 --> 00:26:42,183
Even if he composed the piece, I don't care!

388
00:26:43,101 --> 00:26:43,935
At this rate,

389
00:26:44,769 --> 00:26:46,479
it will be a disaster for both of you.

390
00:26:46,563 --> 00:26:47,397
It'll be so bad, you--

391
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:48,356
Enough!

392
00:26:50,108 --> 00:26:53,737
I told you I'll handle it. Why stick your nose where it doesn't belong?!

393
00:27:02,829 --> 00:27:03,830
I'm sorry, Jae-in…

394
00:27:05,790 --> 00:27:08,251
But I really have to do this performance…

395
00:27:09,878 --> 00:27:11,087
Please stop interfering.

396
00:27:12,672 --> 00:27:14,883
Even if something goes wrong and it's awful…

397
00:27:15,967 --> 00:27:17,469
I'll take take responsibility.

398
00:27:18,553 --> 00:27:19,387
All right?

399
00:27:31,858 --> 00:27:33,652
Is punishment is to be dealt out,

400
00:27:36,112 --> 00:27:37,739
It will definitely come from me.

401
00:27:38,573 --> 00:27:41,326
Just wait. I'm gonna make your life hell.

402
00:27:46,831 --> 00:27:47,666
Jae-in,

403
00:27:48,291 --> 00:27:50,293
can we meet tomorrow? We need to talk.

404
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:53,254
I'll head over to your area.

405
00:27:53,338 --> 00:27:54,422
JAE-IN, CAN WE MEET TOMORROW?

406
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:56,675
WE NEED TO TALK I'LL HEAD OVER TO YOUR AREA

407
00:27:57,592 --> 00:27:58,426
SEND

408
00:28:10,730 --> 00:28:11,564
What?

409
00:28:12,065 --> 00:28:12,899
Are you sorry?

410
00:28:16,611 --> 00:28:17,445
Ooh…

411
00:28:19,364 --> 00:28:20,198
Are you sorry?

412
00:28:22,158 --> 00:28:24,869
Is that why you're incapable of looking me in the eye?

413
00:28:26,329 --> 00:28:28,164
Well… It's okay.

414
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:29,833
I get it.

415
00:28:31,918 --> 00:28:35,130
I know that you get really edgy before a performance.

416
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:37,632
Still,

417
00:28:38,299 --> 00:28:39,509
it was quite hurtful…

418
00:28:39,592 --> 00:28:41,136
when you said I overstepped.

419
00:28:47,767 --> 00:28:49,644
How are your fingers?

420
00:28:51,813 --> 00:28:52,856
Why are you…

421
00:28:53,940 --> 00:28:54,774
so fixated

422
00:28:54,858 --> 00:28:56,192
on Jeong-yo's piece?

423
00:28:57,068 --> 00:28:59,070
You're pushing yourself way too hard.

424
00:28:59,154 --> 00:29:01,489
Did something happen between you two?

425
00:29:02,615 --> 00:29:03,450
Jae-in.

426
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:08,455
I asked you to come here today…

427
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:15,170
because we need to break up.

428
00:29:19,382 --> 00:29:22,594
I've got to fully focus on my music, and you're holding me back.

429
00:29:23,386 --> 00:29:25,263
When I ask myself why I was with you…

430
00:29:25,847 --> 00:29:28,349
I honestly don't think it was because I loved you.

431
00:29:30,268 --> 00:29:31,394
I'm sorry to say this.

432
00:29:34,856 --> 00:29:37,066
You know, you've always been so controlling.

433
00:29:38,985 --> 00:29:40,069
It's suffocating.

434
00:29:42,822 --> 00:29:45,200
I know I probably shouldn't be saying this now,

435
00:29:46,493 --> 00:29:48,912
but you should know how I really feel about you.

436
00:29:51,456 --> 00:29:52,290
I'm sorry…

437
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:56,044
For hurting you like this.

438
00:29:59,714 --> 00:30:00,590
I should just go.

439
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:19,651
What the hell?

440
00:30:21,319 --> 00:30:22,570
You can't just do that.

441
00:30:24,072 --> 00:30:26,282
You tell me that we're done and that's it?

442
00:30:28,701 --> 00:30:29,536
Yeah,

443
00:30:30,203 --> 00:30:32,580
We started dating because I had a crush on you.

444
00:30:32,664 --> 00:30:33,790
You're right.

445
00:30:34,582 --> 00:30:35,667
But you made me feel…

446
00:30:36,417 --> 00:30:38,837
that I was special to you, since we were little.

447
00:30:39,504 --> 00:30:41,130
No, I just needed

448
00:30:42,715 --> 00:30:45,134
someone who would always cheer me on. That's it.

449
00:30:46,219 --> 00:30:47,053
Then…

450
00:30:49,138 --> 00:30:50,306
just tell me the truth.

451
00:30:53,726 --> 00:30:54,561
Did you really…

452
00:30:57,856 --> 00:30:58,940
never love me at all?

453
00:31:00,275 --> 00:31:01,401
Not even for a moment?

454
00:31:03,611 --> 00:31:05,780
No. I never did.

455
00:31:14,330 --> 00:31:15,164
So not at all?

456
00:31:23,673 --> 00:31:24,507
I'm sorry.

457
00:32:05,590 --> 00:32:07,634
EUGENE ART CENTER

458
00:32:16,142 --> 00:32:18,144
There's an awkward tension between them.

459
00:32:18,728 --> 00:32:20,980
Don't you think it could just be nerves though?

460
00:32:21,064 --> 00:32:24,734
I really think something's going on. I just can't put my finger on it.

461
00:32:54,013 --> 00:32:55,181
N

462
00:32:56,307 --> 00:32:57,141
N

463
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:39,392
Okay, let's begin recording.

464
00:33:40,268 --> 00:33:41,102
Take one.

465
00:34:46,375 --> 00:34:47,210
N

466
00:34:54,550 --> 00:34:55,384
Take two.

467
00:35:41,931 --> 00:35:43,516
What was the problem this time?

468
00:35:44,142 --> 00:35:46,519
There wasn't anything wrong this time around.

469
00:35:46,602 --> 00:35:48,354
No, there was actually an issue.

470
00:35:50,064 --> 00:35:53,234
Other people might not have felt it, but I can feel it clearly.

471
00:35:54,443 --> 00:35:56,279
I can feel your anxiety creeping in.

472
00:36:01,450 --> 00:36:02,285
I understand.

473
00:36:02,785 --> 00:36:05,037
I know you're anxious because we're tight on time,

474
00:36:05,121 --> 00:36:07,290
but you should relax and play with ease.

475
00:36:07,957 --> 00:36:08,791
Because if in the end,

476
00:36:08,875 --> 00:36:12,461
it turns out you can't pull this off, none of us are going home either.

477
00:36:14,172 --> 00:36:15,256
Let us go home, okay?

478
00:36:21,262 --> 00:36:22,096
Take three.

479
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:08,309
No. This isn't it.

480
00:37:09,268 --> 00:37:11,354
The tension by now should be at its peak,

481
00:37:12,063 --> 00:37:13,814
-but it's a bit weak. -But I…

482
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:16,567
played it with as much urgency as I possibly could!

483
00:37:18,194 --> 00:37:19,028
Oh, no.

484
00:37:19,695 --> 00:37:23,032
You just moved your fingers as quickly as possible on the piano.

485
00:37:23,574 --> 00:37:26,285
But not once did your emotion ever reach its peak.

486
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:27,453
N

487
00:37:29,872 --> 00:37:30,706
Right here.

488
00:37:30,790 --> 00:37:33,000
Why do you think I wrote this part like this?

489
00:37:33,084 --> 00:37:36,629
I used eighth-note and sixteenth-note triplets to express the fear of death

490
00:37:36,712 --> 00:37:38,506
drawing closer by the second.

491
00:37:38,589 --> 00:37:39,590
And right here!

492
00:37:41,926 --> 00:37:45,137
I used marcato to capture the emotions of betrayal and revenge.

493
00:37:45,221 --> 00:37:46,430
But…

494
00:37:47,848 --> 00:37:51,185
do you actually think your performance is conveying all of those emotions?

495
00:37:51,269 --> 00:37:52,520
No, not in the slightest!

496
00:37:56,023 --> 00:37:56,857
Are you avoiding

497
00:37:57,483 --> 00:38:00,152
those deep emotions because they're too overwhelming?

498
00:38:00,736 --> 00:38:02,071
I've told you this before.

499
00:38:02,571 --> 00:38:04,949
The scenery the composer saw, the emotions he felt…

500
00:38:05,032 --> 00:38:07,618
Capture and express them as they were written down.

501
00:38:08,661 --> 00:38:09,912
But all this time,

502
00:38:09,996 --> 00:38:11,664
all you've done, is retreat.

503
00:38:12,248 --> 00:38:13,082
N

504
00:38:13,165 --> 00:38:15,668
You better stop avoiding it and face it right now!

505
00:38:18,587 --> 00:38:21,215
Stop making things harder for everyone.

506
00:38:22,633 --> 00:38:24,051
Just put your heart into it!

507
00:38:25,511 --> 00:38:27,805
I sincerely hope you make it work this time around.

508
00:38:27,888 --> 00:38:29,223
Give into it, will you?

509
00:38:33,811 --> 00:38:35,479
Take twenty-seven.

510
00:38:52,496 --> 00:38:54,248
Everything I did, I did it for you.

511
00:38:54,957 --> 00:38:55,833
So you could win.

512
00:38:57,251 --> 00:38:59,170
Would you just listen to yourself!

513
00:39:15,227 --> 00:39:16,937
You know… there… were these rumors

514
00:39:17,021 --> 00:39:21,108
going around that you were involved with Choi Jong-yo's disappearance somehow.

515
00:39:22,985 --> 00:39:25,404
What's up with that rumor regarding Choi Jeong-yo?

516
00:39:25,488 --> 00:39:29,158
What exactly happened with that? I heard you had something to do with it.

517
00:39:58,312 --> 00:39:59,146
What's wrong?

518
00:40:01,482 --> 00:40:03,067
What is it? Can't move your fingers?

519
00:40:03,150 --> 00:40:03,984
N

520
00:40:05,403 --> 00:40:06,237
I can't…

521
00:40:06,904 --> 00:40:08,823
I was hoping it wouldn't come to this…

522
00:40:10,282 --> 00:40:13,411
It's my fault. I overestimated what you were capable of doing.

523
00:40:13,994 --> 00:40:16,497
My biggest mistake was giving you this piece.

524
00:40:17,623 --> 00:40:19,375
I'm sorry to say, but you're fired.

525
00:40:21,419 --> 00:40:23,212
Well… Everybody…

526
00:40:24,171 --> 00:40:25,339
I'm sorry to say,

527
00:40:25,840 --> 00:40:27,174
but the recording is over.

528
00:40:39,353 --> 00:40:41,730
I'm sorry, but we're going to take a short break.

529
00:40:41,814 --> 00:40:42,773
Just for a moment.

530
00:40:58,372 --> 00:40:59,206
Hey.

531
00:41:00,791 --> 00:41:02,585
This was what you planned, wasn't it?

532
00:41:02,668 --> 00:41:06,088
Why not expose everything and quit playing games with me already.

533
00:41:06,172 --> 00:41:08,549
I'll take whatever punishment I deserve,

534
00:41:08,632 --> 00:41:10,593
so why not just tell everyone already?

535
00:41:10,676 --> 00:41:11,635
N

536
00:41:12,636 --> 00:41:13,471
You didn't know?

537
00:41:14,180 --> 00:41:15,014
I'd do this?

538
00:41:16,098 --> 00:41:16,974
But I told you,

539
00:41:17,683 --> 00:41:20,311
that all that pain, anger, and betrayal I felt…

540
00:41:21,187 --> 00:41:22,855
I would make you feel it too.

541
00:41:28,277 --> 00:41:29,111
But…

542
00:41:30,070 --> 00:41:32,615
a part of me is disappointed in you, Kang Pi-o.

543
00:41:33,991 --> 00:41:37,161
I was actually curious to see if you could go past your limits.

544
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:39,413
I…

545
00:41:40,706 --> 00:41:41,874
had high hopes for you.

546
00:41:47,963 --> 00:41:48,797
Truth be told,

547
00:41:49,757 --> 00:41:51,842
you're nothing more than a pathetic loser

548
00:41:52,426 --> 00:41:55,137
who shouldn't have gone into music in the first place.

549
00:41:56,222 --> 00:41:59,517
It's people like you who tear real geniuses down out of jealousy.

550
00:42:06,273 --> 00:42:07,900
With pathetic skills like yours,

551
00:42:09,026 --> 00:42:12,154
how dare you claim first place by destroying my life?

552
00:42:14,865 --> 00:42:15,699
Yeah.

553
00:42:21,038 --> 00:42:22,373
You will never beat me.

554
00:42:32,758 --> 00:42:33,592
Pi-o.

555
00:42:34,426 --> 00:42:35,261
Pi-o.

556
00:42:36,345 --> 00:42:38,472
Quickly, where's the key? Hurry, find it!

557
00:42:38,973 --> 00:42:39,974
Hurry up!

558
00:42:44,436 --> 00:42:45,271
There.

559
00:43:04,665 --> 00:43:05,499
N

560
00:43:05,583 --> 00:43:08,168
I told you not to trust him, why didn't you listen?

561
00:43:11,714 --> 00:43:12,548
Look at them.

562
00:43:15,759 --> 00:43:17,845
I… I would like to apologize.

563
00:43:18,554 --> 00:43:19,388
Pianist Kang Pi-o

564
00:43:19,471 --> 00:43:23,392
wasn't quite able to convey what I had intended as the composer of the piece.

565
00:43:23,475 --> 00:43:26,228
I realize now that I should've changed course sooner.

566
00:43:27,104 --> 00:43:28,314
I take full responsibility.

567
00:43:28,397 --> 00:43:30,190
I'm not sure. N

568
00:43:30,691 --> 00:43:31,692
Was it really

569
00:43:32,443 --> 00:43:34,278
Pianist Kang Pi-o who was the issue?

570
00:43:34,778 --> 00:43:35,613
How I see it,

571
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:38,032
the way you were communicating

572
00:43:38,115 --> 00:43:40,743
with your soloist is what completely derailed him.

573
00:43:41,952 --> 00:43:45,080
You forced him to practice nonstop, and kept tearing him down.

574
00:43:45,956 --> 00:43:47,666
The performer was so intimidated

575
00:43:47,750 --> 00:43:49,084
that he eventually fell apart.

576
00:43:49,168 --> 00:43:50,794
Hong Jae-in, cut it out, please.

577
00:43:52,838 --> 00:43:55,132
The soloist was mentally too weak to handle the piece.

578
00:43:55,215 --> 00:43:56,925
Why are you blaming the composer?

579
00:43:57,009 --> 00:43:57,968
I can't believe it.

580
00:43:59,845 --> 00:44:01,096
If we just think for a minute,

581
00:44:01,180 --> 00:44:03,891
it's obvious that he hadn't yet overcome his slump.

582
00:44:04,516 --> 00:44:06,810
We were so caught up in his previous success

583
00:44:06,894 --> 00:44:08,729
that we ignored all of the signs.

584
00:44:09,647 --> 00:44:10,522
I don't think so.

585
00:44:11,482 --> 00:44:13,734
I heard it, he was playing incredibly well.

586
00:44:15,694 --> 00:44:16,695
That doesn't matter.

587
00:44:18,113 --> 00:44:18,947
Kang Pi-o…

588
00:44:19,865 --> 00:44:23,535
is the one responsible for ruining that very expensive recording session.

589
00:44:24,536 --> 00:44:28,207
No matter how good he is offstage, if he can't keep his head clear on stage,

590
00:44:28,290 --> 00:44:29,166
that alone proves

591
00:44:29,958 --> 00:44:31,335
he shouldn't be performing.

592
00:44:32,336 --> 00:44:33,170
Well,

593
00:44:33,671 --> 00:44:35,756
the anniversary concert is right around the corner.

594
00:44:35,839 --> 00:44:37,132
Let's forget the album.

595
00:44:37,675 --> 00:44:39,259
What about the performance?

596
00:44:39,343 --> 00:44:42,388
On the off chance that something like this would happen,

597
00:44:42,471 --> 00:44:44,473
I had another musician in mind.

598
00:44:46,308 --> 00:44:47,976
How about Pianist Lee Min-sung?

599
00:44:49,436 --> 00:44:50,270
Lee Min-sung…

600
00:44:52,189 --> 00:44:54,066
Lee Min-sung, Lee Min-sung…

601
00:44:58,654 --> 00:45:00,197
INCOMING CALL JAE-IN

602
00:45:04,326 --> 00:45:06,286
TVM NEWS, KANG PI-O SUFFERS FROM STAGE FRIGHT AGAIN…

603
00:45:06,370 --> 00:45:09,623
REPLACED BY PIANIST LEE MIN-SUNG FOR 80TH ANNIVERSARY PERFORMANCE

604
00:45:14,878 --> 00:45:18,590
KANG PI-O HAS HAD DIFFICULTY PERFORMING AS USUAL DURING RECENT REHEARSALS…

605
00:45:25,305 --> 00:45:26,473
My apologies, Mr. Kang.

606
00:45:27,057 --> 00:45:29,977
You did tell me that this piece wasn't right for Mr. Kang Pi-o,

607
00:45:30,060 --> 00:45:31,186
and I still pushed it.

608
00:45:31,729 --> 00:45:33,522
I was being too stubborn, I see it now.

609
00:45:33,605 --> 00:45:35,691
I'm really sorry for making you worry.

610
00:45:37,526 --> 00:45:40,404
If that's what the composer says, then that's what it is.

611
00:45:40,487 --> 00:45:41,613
Choi Jeong-yo,

612
00:45:42,322 --> 00:45:45,576
do you remember what I tried to tell you before about that piece?

613
00:45:46,785 --> 00:45:47,619
I wanted the

614
00:45:47,703 --> 00:45:51,623
performance to bring the piece to life in a way that would speak to everybody.

615
00:45:52,374 --> 00:45:53,834
And did you end up doing that?

616
00:45:53,917 --> 00:45:55,252
N

617
00:45:56,086 --> 00:45:57,755
-You see… -N

618
00:45:57,838 --> 00:46:01,967
I have a feeling that your intentions behind this piece weren't entirely pure.

619
00:46:02,509 --> 00:46:03,385
And why is that?

620
00:46:04,219 --> 00:46:05,053
I don't know.

621
00:46:07,514 --> 00:46:10,684
I just composed the most personal piece I could possibly write.

622
00:46:18,859 --> 00:46:19,693
-Hm. -Here.

623
00:46:21,236 --> 00:46:22,070
N

624
00:46:22,154 --> 00:46:24,156
-I'm sorry for coming to see you -N

625
00:46:24,907 --> 00:46:25,741
all of a sudden.

626
00:46:28,660 --> 00:46:29,495
But…

627
00:46:30,204 --> 00:46:31,371
I'm just really upset.

628
00:46:32,581 --> 00:46:34,500
And there's no one else I can talk to.

629
00:46:35,417 --> 00:46:37,294
Don't you worry about it. It's okay.

630
00:46:37,377 --> 00:46:38,462
You can tell me anything.

631
00:46:38,545 --> 00:46:39,379
Mm -hmm.

632
00:46:41,381 --> 00:46:42,299
There's something…

633
00:46:43,467 --> 00:46:44,927
going on between those two.

634
00:46:46,303 --> 00:46:50,265
I saw it… I saw how Pi-o was being treated deliberately harsher

635
00:46:51,391 --> 00:46:53,352
than how he treated everyone else.

636
00:46:54,102 --> 00:46:55,562
As for Pi-o, N

637
00:46:55,646 --> 00:46:57,105
he's not saying anything.

638
00:46:57,189 --> 00:46:59,066
I don't know what's going on.

639
00:46:59,149 --> 00:47:02,194
You know, Jeong-yo being the conductor and the composer of the piece

640
00:47:02,277 --> 00:47:04,822
of course, he's gonna be ambitious. That said--

641
00:47:04,905 --> 00:47:07,825
I'm very well aware of that. But I'm telling you, to me…

642
00:47:08,367 --> 00:47:11,203
it seems like he's really doing it on purpose.

643
00:47:14,414 --> 00:47:15,874
It looks like… N

644
00:47:17,668 --> 00:47:19,628
he is deliberately trying to ruin Pi-o.

645
00:47:24,508 --> 00:47:26,093
Can you please save my Pi-o?

646
00:47:28,053 --> 00:47:30,430
Please get Choi Jeong-yo away him.

647
00:47:30,931 --> 00:47:32,140
I'm so scared.

648
00:47:33,517 --> 00:47:34,852
I'm scared to death.

649
00:47:44,361 --> 00:47:46,113
If you ever need any help, call me.

650
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:53,453
PERSONAL ISSUES CONSULTING

651
00:47:53,537 --> 00:47:54,913
KIM SE-JIN 010.0542.3167

652
00:47:56,957 --> 00:47:58,417
INCOMING CALL HYUN-SOO

653
00:48:00,377 --> 00:48:01,211
Ugh…

654
00:48:03,755 --> 00:48:05,591
-What do you want? -I need to see you.

655
00:48:05,674 --> 00:48:06,675
Where are you?

656
00:48:06,758 --> 00:48:08,343
I'm kind of busy right now, I can't--

657
00:48:08,427 --> 00:48:10,137
We need to meet. It's about Pi-o.

658
00:48:20,230 --> 00:48:21,148
What's this about?

659
00:48:22,399 --> 00:48:24,818
Is it about him being replaced for the concerto?

660
00:48:25,777 --> 00:48:27,571
That was all Choi Jeong-yo's doing.

661
00:48:28,530 --> 00:48:29,781
Pi-o was just being used.

662
00:48:31,116 --> 00:48:31,950
Why?

663
00:48:35,287 --> 00:48:37,539
Why would Jeong-yo do something like that?

664
00:48:38,999 --> 00:48:39,833
Who knows.

665
00:48:41,418 --> 00:48:44,755
Maybe he thought Pi-o was living his best life while he was gone.

666
00:48:45,422 --> 00:48:46,798
Maybe he was jealous of him.

667
00:48:46,882 --> 00:48:47,716
Or…

668
00:48:48,634 --> 00:48:49,468
something of the sort.

669
00:48:49,551 --> 00:48:53,847
That's not it, Ji-hye. Uh… You know that's not the case at all!

670
00:48:56,725 --> 00:48:59,019
Please, can you just tell me the truth already.

671
00:48:59,102 --> 00:49:00,938
Tell me what happened back then. Come on.

672
00:49:01,021 --> 00:49:03,357
The disturbing rumor that was going around…

673
00:49:03,440 --> 00:49:06,485
Of Pi-o having been involved in Jeong-yo's disappearance.

674
00:49:06,568 --> 00:49:08,236
Was that actually true?

675
00:49:09,655 --> 00:49:10,489
How can you say…

676
00:49:13,367 --> 00:49:14,242
It's not true.

677
00:49:17,996 --> 00:49:20,332
How could you believe something so ridiculous?

678
00:49:23,043 --> 00:49:23,877
I'm leaving.

679
00:49:25,712 --> 00:49:28,173
And the things you said to me? What was that about?

680
00:49:28,256 --> 00:49:31,176
You asked me to keep Pi-o away from Jeong-yo!

681
00:49:31,927 --> 00:49:33,720
You told me you were scared to death!

682
00:49:33,804 --> 00:49:35,097
Why the hell say that?

683
00:49:44,189 --> 00:49:47,693
But as it turns out, you're just a pathetic loser consumed by your own

684
00:49:47,776 --> 00:49:51,238
inferiority, who never should've pursued music in the first place.

685
00:49:52,739 --> 00:49:56,368
It's jealous people like you who drive real real geniuses to the ground.

686
00:50:04,084 --> 00:50:04,918
He didn't do it.

687
00:50:07,629 --> 00:50:10,632
I'm telling you, Pi-o didn't do it. Pi-o…

688
00:50:12,217 --> 00:50:13,635
he didn't do anything wrong.

689
00:50:14,511 --> 00:50:15,345
It was all…

690
00:50:17,472 --> 00:50:18,306
It was…

691
00:50:20,475 --> 00:50:21,560
It was all my doing.

692
00:50:24,354 --> 00:50:25,188
I…

693
00:50:28,066 --> 00:50:29,317
I was the one who did it.

694
00:50:56,845 --> 00:50:57,721
N

695
00:50:57,804 --> 00:50:58,847
N

696
00:51:10,358 --> 00:51:11,193
N

697
00:51:12,652 --> 00:51:13,487
N

698
00:52:14,089 --> 00:52:14,923
Grandad.

699
00:52:16,508 --> 00:52:17,467
Is it unbearable?

700
00:52:29,896 --> 00:52:31,815
That is just the nature of art.

701
00:52:35,235 --> 00:52:38,196
We might as well be trying to pluck the stars from the sky.

702
00:52:39,197 --> 00:52:41,199
Like a mirage you can never quite grasp.

703
00:52:42,200 --> 00:52:44,744
You chase after it, and there it is in the distance.

704
00:52:44,828 --> 00:52:46,288
You chase after it again,

705
00:52:46,371 --> 00:52:47,998
and it's farther out of reach.

706
00:52:52,377 --> 00:52:55,380
Even so, do you still want to take this windy, thorny path?

707
00:52:57,924 --> 00:53:01,136
Say you had less than a month to live, would you still want to

708
00:53:02,012 --> 00:53:04,097
keep playing the piano till the very end?

709
00:53:16,651 --> 00:53:17,485
Yes.

710
00:53:18,111 --> 00:53:19,070
I definitely would.

711
00:53:20,655 --> 00:53:22,574
I know that I'm still not good enough…

712
00:53:24,868 --> 00:53:27,204
The piano is the one thing that brings me joy.

713
00:53:28,121 --> 00:53:28,955
Even if…

714
00:53:30,582 --> 00:53:32,459
I only had one more day left to live,

715
00:53:33,835 --> 00:53:35,712
I would still want to play the piano.

716
00:54:28,807 --> 00:54:30,058
Change things, Kang Pi-o.

717
00:54:31,476 --> 00:54:33,687
Stop relying on a contraption like that.

718
00:54:33,770 --> 00:54:36,690
And draw out the natural sense of rhythm you carry inside.

719
00:54:40,944 --> 00:54:44,114
A soloist must never lose the drive to keep pushing forward.

720
00:54:45,198 --> 00:54:47,409
Command the stage with your own energy.

721
00:54:47,492 --> 00:54:49,452
If your energy is strong enough,

722
00:54:49,536 --> 00:54:51,496
you can pull the entire orchestra

723
00:54:51,579 --> 00:54:53,790
and the conductor into your own world.

724
00:54:59,587 --> 00:55:00,547
Looking back,

725
00:55:01,673 --> 00:55:04,092
music that moves people, deeply in their hearts

726
00:55:04,926 --> 00:55:07,095
is music that carries a lifetime within it.

727
00:55:08,638 --> 00:55:09,472
So…

728
00:55:10,348 --> 00:55:13,601
your desire to make music even with only one day left to live

729
00:55:14,102 --> 00:55:14,936
is what matters.

730
00:55:17,355 --> 00:55:18,440
Put it in your music.

731
00:55:32,120 --> 00:55:33,038
Do you understand?

732
00:55:42,505 --> 00:55:43,340
N

733
00:55:47,260 --> 00:55:48,303
N

734
00:55:52,223 --> 00:55:53,058
Conductor Choi.

735
00:55:54,017 --> 00:55:55,018
Let me introduce you.

736
00:55:55,101 --> 00:55:56,394
This is Pianist Lee Min-sung,

737
00:55:56,478 --> 00:55:59,439
whom we went to great lengths to get on board for your piece.

738
00:55:59,522 --> 00:56:00,607
Hello sir,

739
00:56:00,690 --> 00:56:02,484
it's an honor to finally meet you.

740
00:56:02,567 --> 00:56:04,027
Oh, no, it's all mine.

741
00:56:04,110 --> 00:56:06,196
Thank you for agreeing to perform with me.

742
00:56:06,279 --> 00:56:07,280
Please, take a seat.

743
00:56:09,949 --> 00:56:13,078
I didn't have much time to practice given the tight timeline.

744
00:56:13,161 --> 00:56:15,330
Can I show you what I've got?

745
00:56:15,413 --> 00:56:16,373
Please do.

746
00:56:16,873 --> 00:56:18,249
N I'm eager to hear it.

747
00:57:12,762 --> 00:57:13,596
N

748
00:57:23,940 --> 00:57:25,567
This is a picture of that woman.

749
00:57:26,776 --> 00:57:27,610
And this…

750
00:57:28,945 --> 00:57:29,821
I'm sorry.

751
00:57:31,406 --> 00:57:32,240
You're right.

752
00:57:33,658 --> 00:57:34,492
I did it.

753
00:57:35,368 --> 00:57:38,997
After I hurt my finger after the final round, I couldn't think straight.

754
00:57:39,789 --> 00:57:42,041
I poured everything I had into winning that competition,

755
00:57:42,125 --> 00:57:44,878
and I was afraid I wouldn't place first because of you.

756
00:57:47,881 --> 00:57:48,715
N

757
00:57:53,636 --> 00:57:56,556
Now… we have everything we need to take these people down.

758
00:57:57,974 --> 00:57:59,934
So now… that Kang Pi-o is shattered,

759
00:58:00,435 --> 00:58:01,811
I'll just put it out there?

760
00:58:02,937 --> 00:58:03,771
Hey?

761
00:58:05,815 --> 00:58:07,775
Oh… 'Kay…

762
00:58:07,859 --> 00:58:08,818
do that.

763
00:58:10,069 --> 00:58:12,030
When the timing is right, I'll call you.

764
00:58:12,113 --> 00:58:13,072
N

765
00:58:13,156 --> 00:58:14,407
Okay, I got you.

766
00:58:14,491 --> 00:58:16,743
So I'll… take you home?

767
00:58:16,826 --> 00:58:17,869
Hm?

768
00:58:32,175 --> 00:58:33,009
Good night, man!

769
00:58:33,635 --> 00:58:34,469
Good night.

770
00:59:00,912 --> 00:59:02,121
What are you doing here?

771
00:59:08,753 --> 00:59:09,587
Choi Jeong-yo.

772
00:59:13,216 --> 00:59:14,634
Just give me another shot.

773
00:59:14,717 --> 00:59:16,302
N N

774
00:59:18,096 --> 00:59:18,930
The solo.

775
00:59:20,765 --> 00:59:22,141
You've got to let me do it.

776
00:59:26,896 --> 00:59:27,855
I'll never do that.

777
00:59:31,651 --> 00:59:32,777
That piece was written

778
00:59:33,861 --> 00:59:35,738
out of your hatred for me, wasn't it?

779
00:59:36,739 --> 00:59:37,740
Do you really think…

780
00:59:38,366 --> 00:59:40,285
that anyone else could play it but me?

781
00:59:41,369 --> 00:59:42,203
N

782
00:59:45,623 --> 00:59:46,916
I'd like… to thank you.

783
00:59:48,084 --> 00:59:50,461
Because going through this, I realized my own limitations.

784
00:59:50,545 --> 00:59:53,047
But… when it comes to "Nemesis",

785
00:59:54,507 --> 00:59:56,759
I'm the only one who can do it justice.

786
01:00:00,138 --> 01:00:01,848
You'll throw away this opportunity

787
01:00:02,807 --> 01:00:04,267
just for the sake of revenge?

788
01:00:35,673 --> 01:00:37,342
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

789
01:00:37,842 --> 01:00:38,968
Do you

790
01:00:39,052 --> 01:00:42,889
believe that a morally flawed artist is fundamentally unworthy of creating art?

791
01:00:42,972 --> 01:00:46,225
Or do you think art and the artist's private life should be judged separately?

792
01:00:46,309 --> 01:00:50,521
Are you here to pass judgement on other people, or are you here to be a musician?

793
01:00:50,605 --> 01:00:52,774
If you'd only given Pi-o the recognition he deserved,

794
01:00:52,857 --> 01:00:55,610
I would never have done any of this! Why did you do that?

795
01:00:55,693 --> 01:00:56,527
HYUN-CHUL

796
01:00:56,611 --> 01:00:58,363
"Why aren't you answering? When do we go public?"

797
01:00:58,446 --> 01:00:59,947
No one touches him but me.

798
01:01:00,823 --> 01:01:01,741
Just admit it already.

799
01:01:01,824 --> 01:01:03,993
I'm the only one who can do this piece justice.

800
01:01:04,077 --> 01:01:05,328
We both know that's true.
